kernelbase: keep Chromium-based programs' drawing in their main process, in software

Launchers built on CEF or Electron draw from a GPU process into the main process's window.
DXMT cannot present into another process's window, and the Mac driver cannot paint one with
GDI from another process either, so the window stays blank. A process that has Chromium in it
(libcef.dll loaded; or ffmpeg.dll imported with Chromium's resources beside the program) gets
--in-process-gpu --disable-gpu --disable-gpu-compositing added to its own command line, unless
it is one of Chromium's child processes. It is done inside the process: adding the switches
when a program is started hits every program in the folder (a launcher's 7z.exe failed on
them). FINEWINE_CHROMIUM_FLAGS names other switches, or "none".

